#: ../../how-to/migration.md:1 da2bd9bb0a304582a0b6ac296e9d3a90
msgid "Migrating to GWexpy v0.1.1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/migration.md:3 54832ca15ec2498a97eb0fca3f6e480c
msgid ""
"This guide summarizes the breaking changes introduced in `v0.1.1` and "
"provides migration paths for existing code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/migration.md:5 797e3f248f494eeea87cd9f6a2a3970d
msgid "1. Lorentzian Peak Parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/migration.md:7 acb109fdb0a54f1d9bf9435016e04aa6
msgid ""
"The `fwhm` (Full Width at Half Maximum) parameter in "
"`gwexpy.noise.peaks.lorentzian_line()` has been renamed to `gamma` (Half "
"Width at Half Maximum) to better align with the underlying mathematical "
"implementation and typical spectral modeling conventions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/migration.md:9 ../../how-to/migration.md:29
#: ../../how-to/migration.md:49 055ef8506a5045868bf7fa75cf7e51a1
#: 999048ad8d734d09a44fb5a66e0af066 da06c467ca2041d692ab3d36e6be6292
msgid "How to Migrate"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/migration.md:10 fc44d66acaf1492a834ebaeaf7e1267a
msgid ""
"If you were using `fwhm`, simply divide your value by 2 and pass it as "
"`gamma`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/migration.md:12 ../../how-to/migration.md:32
#: ../../how-to/migration.md:52 0d25ffd9139549a4ac0f290d335000d1
#: 77c3f95393614801a300704545b61982 ac643e41ae924d89a98988c46108ac4d
msgid "**Old (v0.1.0):**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/migration.md:18 ../../how-to/migration.md:38
#: ../../how-to/migration.md:59 1f4e426ba9f342e685ef30136c6c9f03
#: 25fa5310d89d43c49254b6b47fdb2948 a4324022426d467ca5bd6872b2344d17
msgid "**New (v0.1.1):**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/migration.md:25 10b956bf12d4421eab99902475fd2c5d
msgid "2. Spectral Fitting (Generalized Least Squares)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/migration.md:27 0757a1290fb045138b63403ca4ffece8
msgid ""
"The `stride` parameter has been removed from `fit_bootstrap_spectrum()` "
"as it was an unsupported keyword argument that caused errors in the "
"underlying `scipy.signal.periodogram` calls."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/migration.md:30 3920fab19bcb424983e3bfc01bd1c748
msgid ""
"Simply remove the `stride` keyword argument from your "
"`fit_bootstrap_spectrum` calls. The function now correctly manages data "
"segmentation through `fftlength` and `overlap`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/migration.md:45 c107aa0246534edf81421d9439e73466
msgid "3. SegmentTable Lazy Loading"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/migration.md:47 0e69c59b42934886a19bc610e92982a2
msgid ""
"The `loader` argument in `SegmentTable.add_series_column()` now expects a"
" callable that takes a single `segment` argument (`loader(segment)`), "
"rather than a factory that takes an index (`loader(i)`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/migration.md:50 f70ef3f441244996a251f97d63bc3e86
msgid ""
"Update your loader functions to accept the `segment` (span) of the row "
"directly."
msgstr ""

